  "details": "It appears what causes Chatboxes and Nameplates to be lower than they should be is the state the player is when their avatar loads in for other players.\n\nIf someone's avatar loads in and they are either Crouching or Prone, their chatbox and nameplate will be significantly lower than if they were standing.\n\nWorkaround: If your avatar loaded in for someone else while you were crouching or prone, then make your avatar fully stand up, and then click Reset Avatar to force it to reload and the position will fix for everyone else.\n\nNote: This only affects how your chatbox looks for others. You won't see the effect if you're checking your own chatbox's position. You need two players to see the bug occur.\n\nTests were done with 2 players in Desktop Mode with a variety of avatars.",
